        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.266,
            0.273,
            0.883,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": "4. A student forgot to remove the insulator covering from the connecting wires while making a circuit. If the lamp and the cell are working properly, will the lamp glow?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.266,
            0.334,
            0.882,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "5. Draw a circuit diagram for a simple torch using symbols for electric components."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.377,
            0.413,
            0.396
          ],
          "content": "6. In Fig. 3.18:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.4,
            0.882,
            0.44
          ],
          "content": "(i) If $\\mathsf { S } _ { 2 }$ is in ‘ON’ position, $\\mathsf { S } _ { 1 }$ is in ‘OFF’ position, which lamp(s) will glow?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.442,
            0.882,
            0.482
          ],
          "content": "(ii) If $\\mathsf { S } _ { 2 }$ is in ‘OFF’ position, $\\mathsf { S } _ { 1 }$ is in ‘ON’ position, which lamp(s) will glow?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.29,
            0.485,
            0.882,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": "(iii) If $\\mathsf { S } _ { 1 }$ and $\\mathsf{S}_{2}$ both are in ‘ON’ position, which lamp(s) will glow?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.012,
